From: xmrblocks security audit <security@monerofund.org>
Subject: [PATCH 0006] finding 7: stop disclosing submitted private view keys

The view key a user submits is the highest-value secret this service handles --
it grants permanent visibility of every incoming transaction of that wallet.
It was being disclosed three ways:

  * rendered in full into /checkrawkeyimgs and /checkrawoutputkeys responses
    ("<h4>Viewkey: {{viewkey}}</h4>" in both templates), landing in browser
    cache, history and any intermediate proxy. /myoutputs already masks the key
    before rendering, so this was an inconsistency rather than a decision.
  * written to stderr on parse failure and on key-derivation failure, so keys
    accumulate in the service log.
  * embedded in the "link to this page" shortcut URL, leaking via Referer,
    browser history and access logs. This one needs no feature flag at all.

Introduces a shared mask_secret() helper and routes all of the above through
it. The shortcut now links to the bare form; the previous URL form cannot be
made safe, since the key has to appear in the path for it to work.

Also fixes a precedence bug in the same expression: ?: binds looser than +, so
the concatenation applied only to the /myoutputs branch and the prove page's
shortcut collapsed to the bare string "/prove".

NOTE for the maintainer: templates/checkrawkeyimgs.html:18 and
templates/checkrawoutputkeys.html:16 still say "Viewkey: {{viewkey}}". The value
is now masked so they are safe as-is, but you may prefer to drop the line.
